% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-13 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: pericardial disease with constrictive physiology (right-sided
%   venous-congestion heart failure with a PRESERVED ejection fraction).
%
% The diagnostic puzzle the IR poses (q1-q6): a 53yo man with progressive,
% refractory, reaccumulating RIGHT-SIDED fluid overload (bilateral leg oedema,
% recurrent bilateral transudative pleural effusions, dilated IVC, enlarged right
% chambers) BUT a vigorous, NORMAL/HYPERDYNAMIC left ventricle (EF ~70%, CO
% ~11 L/min). A thickened pericardium (>4.5 mm) with effusion was repeatedly
% under-emphasized and only seen on re-review once the effusion was accounted for;
% the mitral inflow E velocity varies >25% with respiration. A tight diagonal-LAD
% stenosis is explicitly framed as an INCIDENTAL lesion that did NOT respond to
% anti-ischaemic therapy.
%
% The reconciling conclusion the summary foregrounds: systemic venous congestion
% with normal systolic function + thickened pericardium + ventricular
% interdependence (respiratory E variation) = constrictive pericarditis, and
% specifically the EFFUSIVE-CONSTRICTIVE variant, because a thickened, constricting
% pericardium coexists with a persistent effusion that MASKED the classic
% septal bounce / Kussmaul sign.
%
% Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY per adj-lang grammar (lowercase only, no
% leading digits, no uppercase). E.g. ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic),
% pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm), pericardial_thickness measured as a band.
%
% Anti-overfit note: every clause is added because a CITED source supports the
% DIRECTION of its likelihood ratio for that finding in that disease, NOT to make
% this case land on a chosen answer. The discriminators that fire AGAINST the
% tempting mimics (restrictive cardiomyopathy; tuberculous aetiology; the
% incidental coronary lesion) are included with LR<1 wherever a source supports
% the negative direction.
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates among "right-sided congestion + preserved EF" referrals) =====

% rationale: constrictive pericarditis is the prototypical CURABLE cause of a
% right-sided venous-congestion heart-failure syndrome with preserved systolic
% function; uncommon but the unifying lesion this vignette is built around.
prior 0.22 for diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK459314 (Constrictive Pericarditis); Nature Rev Cardiol 2014 nrcardio.2014.100 (curable diastolic HF)" trust authoritative

% rationale: effusive-constrictive pericarditis is the SUBCATEGORY in which a
% constricting (often thickened) pericardium coexists with a tense effusion that
% masks classic constrictive signs — exactly the "effusion obscured the thickened
% pericardium / no clear septal bounce / no Kussmaul" picture here.
prior 0.20 for diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (Constrictive-Effusive Pericarditis); MDPI Hearts 2024 18/1/32 (Kussmaul in effusive-constrictive)" trust authoritative

% rationale: restrictive cardiomyopathy is the single most important MIMIC of
% constriction (same venous congestion + preserved EF) and must be argued down on
% the discriminating data; moderate prior so the engine must EARN the separation.
prior 0.18 for diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 circimaging.113.001613 (CP vs RCM differentiation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: tuberculous pericarditis is a leading WORLD cause of constriction and a
% standing differential whenever a thickened pericardium + serositis is found; on
% the list but testable by effusion ADA.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(tuberculous_pericarditis)
  source "ScienceDirect (Tuberculous Pericarditis overview); PubMed 8665976 (ADA in TB pericarditis)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a primary high-output heart-failure state (obesity, liver disease, AV
% shunt, myeloproliferative) is on the differential because CO ~11 L/min is frankly
% high; competing explanation for the congestion that does NOT need a pericardium.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure)
  source "PMC11307472 Danger High Output; PMC3833917 Living with high output (causes of high-output HF)" trust authoritative

% rationale: coronary artery disease was the PRIOR working diagnosis (treated as
% presumed coronary disease); high-ish prior so the engine must demote it on the
% data that it is incidental and therapy-unresponsive.
prior 0.12 for diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
  source "IR: presumed coronary disease treated with antiplatelet/statin/beta-blocker (prior working dx)" trust inferred

% ===== SHARED RIGHT-SIDED VENOUS-CONGESTION SIGNATURE =====
% rationale: marked pitting lower-limb oedema, recurrent bilateral pleural effusions,
% a dilated IVC and enlarged right chambers are NOT four independent facts — they are
% ONE correlated syndrome of elevated systemic venous / right-atrial pressure. It is
% the shared final common path of BOTH constriction and restriction, so it fires
% ONCE per such conclusion rather than summing four edges (anti-saturation). It does
% NOT by itself separate constriction from restriction — the discriminators below do.
% mechanism systemic_venous_congestion for diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis) lr 4.0 : symptom(marked_pitting_oedema_lower_limbs), symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions), ivc_dilated(over_twenty_mm), right_chambers_enlarged
% mechanism systemic_venous_congestion for diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis) lr 4.0 : symptom(marked_pitting_oedema_lower_limbs), symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions), ivc_dilated(over_twenty_mm), right_chambers_enlarged
% mechanism systemic_venous_congestion for diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy) lr 3.5 : symptom(marked_pitting_oedema_lower_limbs), symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions), ivc_dilated(over_twenty_mm), right_chambers_enlarged
% mechanism systemic_venous_congestion for diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure) lr 2.5 : symptom(marked_pitting_oedema_lower_limbs), symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions), ivc_dilated(over_twenty_mm), right_chambers_enlarged

% ===== CONSTRICTIVE PERICARDITIS (and its effusive-constrictive variant) =====

% rationale: the defining PARADOX — right-sided congestion with a NORMAL/hyperdynamic
% EF — is the cardinal presentation of constriction (venous congestion dominates;
% systolic function is preserved). This is the discriminator that demotes ordinary
% systolic heart failure.
contributes 3.5 from ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "PMC4008396 Chronic Constrictive Pericarditis; PMC7282374 (treatable diastolic HF, preserved EF)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.0 from ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK459314 (constriction: venous congestion with preserved systolic function)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a THICKENED pericardium (>4 mm on CT/MRI) is strongly supportive of
% constriction; on CT >2 mm and on MRI >4 mm are the abnormal thresholds, and a
% measured >4.5 mm clears both.
contributes 3.5 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "PMC4929280; RSNA Radiology 13121059 (CT >2mm / MRI >4mm pericardial thickening in CP)" trust authoritative
% rationale: thickened pericardium that COEXISTS with a persistent effusion is the
% structural hallmark of the EFFUSIVE-constrictive variant specifically.
contributes 4.0 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (effusive-constrictive: thickened/adherent pericardium WITH effusion)" trust authoritative

% rationale: respiratory variation of mitral inflow E velocity >25% is a classic
% sign of ventricular interdependence and is used to distinguish constriction from
% restriction; a well-recognised positive discriminator FOR constriction.
contributes 3.0 from mitral_e_respiratory_variation(over_twenty_five_percent) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (>=25% respiratory mitral E variation in CP); PubMed 24633783 Mayo criteria" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from mitral_e_respiratory_variation(over_twenty_five_percent) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (respiratory mitral E variation, ventricular interdependence)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY for the EFFUSIVE-CONSTRICTIVE variant — a persistent / reaccumulating
% effusion can MASK the septal bounce and Kussmaul sign; so their ABSENCE does NOT
% argue against effusive-constrictive disease and is, if anything, consistent with a
% tense effusion overlying constriction (LR mildly >1 here).
contributes 1.5 from septal_bounce(not_clearly_seen) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579; MDPI Hearts 2024 18/1/32 (effusion masks constrictive signs)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.5 from kussmaul_sign(absent) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (tense effusion can obscure Kussmaul in effusive-constrictive)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — for PURE/classic constriction, a clear
% septal bounce is one of the most sensitive/specific signs; its absence argues
% modestly AGAINST simple non-effusive constriction (and toward the effusive variant).
contributes 0.6 from septal_bounce(not_clearly_seen) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (septal shift/bounce sensitive+specific for constriction)" trust authoritative

% rationale: low pleural-fluid LDH consistent with a TRANSUDATIVE effusion is the
% expected character of a cardiac/venous-congestion effusion, supporting a pericardial
% constrictive (haemodynamic) cause over an inflammatory/exudative one.
contributes 1.6 from pleural_fluid_ldh(low) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "JTD Wijayaratne (cardiac pleural effusions are typically transudative, low LDH)" trust authoritative

% ===== RESTRICTIVE CARDIOMYOPATHY (the principal MIMIC — must be argued DOWN) =====

% rationale: RCM shares the right-sided congestion + preserved EF picture, so the
% congestion mechanism and a preserved EF are mildly supportive of it too.
contributes 1.8 from ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic) to diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (RCM: preserved EF, venous congestion — mimics CP)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — a THICKENED pericardium points to a
% PERICARDIAL process; RCM is a MYOCARDIAL disease with a normal pericardium, so
% pericardial thickening argues against RCM.
contributes 0.25 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy)
  source "RSNA Radiology 13121059; AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (pericardial thickening favours CP over RCM)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — marked respiratory variation of
% mitral inflow E velocity reflects pericardial ventricular interdependence and is
% characteristically ABSENT/blunted in RCM; >25% variation argues against RCM.
contributes 0.3 from mitral_e_respiratory_variation(over_twenty_five_percent) to diagnosis(restrictive_cardiomyopathy)
  source "AHA Circ 1989 79.2.357; Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (respiratory E variation favours CP, not RCM)" trust authoritative

% ===== TUBERCULOUS PERICARDITIS (testable mimic — argued down by effusion ADA) =====

% rationale: a thickened pericardium with effusion is compatible with a tuberculous
% aetiology, the leading infective cause of constriction worldwide.
contributes 1.6 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pericarditis)
  source "ScienceDirect Tuberculous Pericarditis overview (TB: leading cause of pericardial constriction)" trust authoritative

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — a LOW adenosine deaminase in the
% serous fluid (~4 U/L, well below the ~40 U/L TB threshold) argues strongly AGAINST
% a tuberculous aetiology (ADA has ~90% sensitivity for TB pericarditis).
contributes 0.15 from pleural_fluid_adenosine_deaminase(low) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pericarditis)
  source "PubMed 8665976; AHA Circ 1994 89.6.2728 (ADA >=40 U/L in ~75-90% of TB; low ADA argues against TB)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a low-LDH TRANSUDATIVE effusion is atypical for the lymphocytic EXUDATE
% expected in tuberculous serositis — mildly against TB.
contributes 0.6 from pleural_fluid_ldh(low) to diagnosis(tuberculous_pericarditis)
  source "ScienceDirect Tuberculous Pericarditis (TB effusions are exudative, lymphocyte-rich)" trust authoritative

% ===== HIGH-OUTPUT HEART FAILURE (explains high CO but NOT the pericardium) =====

% rationale: a calculated cardiac output ~11 L/min with a large stroke volume is the
% defining feature of a high-output state and is what makes this differential live.
contributes 3.0 from cardiac_output(markedly_elevated) to diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure)
  source "PMC11307472 (high-output HF defined by elevated cardiac output >8 L/min)" trust authoritative
% rationale: mild anaemia is a recognised contributor to / cause of a high-output
% state; supportive but non-specific.
contributes 1.4 from lab(mild_anaemia) to diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure)
  source "PMC3833917 Living with high output (anaemia among high-output drivers)" trust authoritative

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — a primary high-output state does NOT
% produce a thickened, constricting pericardium; pericardial thickening argues against
% high-output HF being the UNIFYING lesion (it cannot explain the structural finding).
contributes 0.4 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to diagnosis(high_output_heart_failure)
  source "PMC4929280 (pericardial thickening is a pericardial-disease finding, not a high-output one)" trust inferred

% rationale: in constriction a raised output with preserved EF can accompany chronic
% volume overload/anaemia; a high CO is therefore NOT incompatible with constriction
% and is weakly consistent with the volume-overloaded constrictive state.
contributes 1.2 from cardiac_output(markedly_elevated) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "PMC4008396 Chronic Constrictive Pericarditis (chronic volume overload, preserved systolic function)" trust inferred

% ===== CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE (the explicit RED HERRING — argued DOWN) =====

% rationale: a CT-angiographic tight diagonal-LAD stenosis is real coronary disease
% and was the basis for the prior working diagnosis; supportive on its face.
contributes 2.0 from cta_finding(tight_stenosis_diagonal_lad) to diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
  source "IR: CT coronary angiography reported a tight diagonal-LAD stenosis" trust inferred

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — chest tightness NOT clearly related
% to exertion is atypical for ischaemic angina and argues against the symptom being
% coronary in origin.
contributes 0.6 from chest_tightness_exertion_relation(not_related) to diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
  source "IR/clinical: non-exertional, come-and-go chest tightness is atypical for ischaemia" trust inferred

% rationale: KEY DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — full anti-ischaemic therapy
% (antiplatelet + statin + beta-blocker) with NO meaningful benefit argues that the
% coronary lesion is incidental rather than the driver of the syndrome.
contributes 0.3 from coronary_treatment_response(no_benefit) to diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
  source "IR: presumed-coronary therapy gave no meaningful benefit (lesion behaves as incidental)" trust inferred

% rationale: DISCRIMINATOR (fires negative) — bilateral right-sided fluid overload with
% recurrent transudative effusions is not a presentation of stable coronary disease;
% it argues against CAD being the unifying cause.
contributes 0.4 from symptom(recurrent_bilateral_pleural_effusions) to diagnosis(coronary_artery_disease)
  source "JTD Wijayaratne (recurrent transudative polyserositis is a congestive, not ischaemic, picture)" trust inferred

% ===== NEXT STEP (confirmatory pathway) =====

% rationale: invasive simultaneous LV/RV catheterisation is the haemodynamic gold
% standard — demonstrating discordant respiratory LV/RV systolic pressure variation
% (ventricular interdependence) and equalised diastolic pressures confirms constriction
% AND distinguishes it from restriction; it also separates effusive-constrictive (where
% pressures persist after pericardiocentesis) from simple tamponade.
prior 0.30 for next_step(invasive_haemodynamic_catheterisation)
  source "Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014; StatPearls NBK519579 (cath: ventricular interdependence confirms constriction)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.5 from mitral_e_respiratory_variation(over_twenty_five_percent) to next_step(invasive_haemodynamic_catheterisation)
  source "AHA Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (echo interdependence -> confirm with invasive interdependence on cath)" trust authoritative
contributes 3.0 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to next_step(invasive_haemodynamic_catheterisation)
  source "RSNA Radiology 13121059 (thickened pericardium + congestion -> confirm constriction haemodynamically)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from ejection_fraction(preserved_hyperdynamic) to next_step(invasive_haemodynamic_catheterisation)
  source "PMC7282374 (preserved-EF congestion is the constriction phenotype warranting confirmation)" trust authoritative

% rationale: dedicated cardiac MRI with late gadolinium enhancement / real-time cine is
% the alternative confirmatory arm — it grades pericardial thickening, shows real-time
% septal interdependence, and LGE flags reversible (inflammatory) constriction that may
% respond to anti-inflammatory therapy before pericardiectomy.
prior 0.18 for next_step(cardiac_mri_with_late_gadolinium)
  source "PMC12985800; Methodist DeBakey CVJ mdcvj.1779 (MRI: thickness, real-time interdependence, LGE reversibility)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from pericardium_thickness(over_four_mm) to next_step(cardiac_mri_with_late_gadolinium)
  source "RSNA RadioGraphics rg.23si035504 (MRI characterises pericardial thickening + inflammation)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved) =====

% u-cath: simultaneous LV/RV catheterisation has not been done; demonstrating (or
% failing to demonstrate) ventricular interdependence is the decisive discriminator
% between constriction and restriction. Each result moves the constriction posterior.
contributes 8.0 from cath_interdependence(present) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (discordant RV/LV systolic pressures = ventricular interdependence, confirms CP)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.12 from cath_interdependence(absent) to diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014 (absence of interdependence argues against constriction, toward RCM)" trust authoritative
uncertain { cath_interdependence(present), cath_interdependence(absent) } for diagnosis(constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "Circ Cardiovasc Imaging 2014; StatPearls NBK459314 (cath interdependence not yet obtained; decisive)"

% u-effusion-persist: whether right-heart filling pressures PERSIST after the effusion
% is drained is the test that defines the EFFUSIVE-CONSTRICTIVE variant (vs simple
% tamponade); the rapid reaccumulation + only transient relief on thoracentesis hints
% at it but the pericardial pressure response is untested.
contributes 6.0 from post_drainage_filling(persistently_elevated) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (persistent elevated RA pressure after pericardiocentesis defines effusive-constrictive)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.2 from post_drainage_filling(normalises) to diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (normalisation after drainage = simple effusion/tamponade, not constriction)" trust authoritative
uncertain { post_drainage_filling(persistently_elevated), post_drainage_filling(normalises) } for diagnosis(effusive_constrictive_pericarditis)
  source "StatPearls NBK519579 (post-pericardiocentesis filling-pressure response not yet measured; defines the variant)"
